WEBVTT

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.330
Here I am, talking to you 
again like this today.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:20.160
What I longed for was a peaceful 
world where I could live

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.410
without harboring anxiety.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.200
Yet... I knew that was a dream 
that wouldn't come true.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.130
So...

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:36.150
I should at least be allowed to dream.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:48.330
<i>My heartbeat resonates through the sky,</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.920
<i>through endless, repeating days,</i>

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.200
<i>as I carry my hidden wounds.</i>

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:15.190
<i>The only freedom I'm allowed</i>

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:21.140
<i>is wandering.</i>

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.700
<i>So since you're here,</i>

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:32.320
<i>I want you to play your harmony for me.</i>

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.030
<i>It's like a brilliant ocean,</i>

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:44.080
<i>the spilling colors melting away.</i>

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.990
<i>Close your eyes, close your eyes.</i>

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.750
<i>It's all right now.</i>

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.050
In the end, our lives

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.920
are possibly nothing more than 
stories woven in between dreams.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.530
Don't you think so, μ?

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.010
<i>A newly released song from μ has 
made it to this week's charts!</i>

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:12.190
<i>The sentiments packed in this song...</i>

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.570
<b>Social Psychology</b>

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.170
Good morning, Shikishima-kun.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.780
Good morning, Mizuguchi-san.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.220
What are you reading there?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.350
Hmm, math?

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.000
No, psychology.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.290
Again?!

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.460
Is the human mind really that interesting?

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.360
I don't get it.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.760
This is called a Johari Window.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.890
It's an exercise to expand 
one's unseen possibilities,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.470
or in other words, to learn one's true self.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.830
It compares aspects of your 
personality to a window.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.900
Hmm, a window?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.360
The rows of the window show whether 
you understand yourself or not.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.830
The columns show whether others 
understand you or not.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.600
This makes four windows:

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.580
the open, the blind, the hidden, 
and the unknown.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.460
Uh-huh.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.550
By revealing more of yourself to others 
or learning what others think of you,

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.430
you can expand the open.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.930
In doing so, you gain awareness of 
aspects even the self hasn't noticed.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.020
Well? Interesting, right?

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.080
The stuff you're talking 
about is complicated.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.180
Is it?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.520
It is. Also...

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:39.360
The hidden?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.740
Couldn't that be something 
even you don't want to know?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.070
<i>The train will be arriving 
momentarily on platform two.</i>

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:53.180
<i>For your safety, please stand back.</i>

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.560
<i>The doors are now closing.</i>

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.680
<i>Please refrain from running onto the train.</i>

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.300
Miyabi Municipal Kishimai High School

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.230
Hey, look! This, this!

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.540
What? What is it, Takatsu?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.110
See!

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.980
μ's new song!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.850
That's the one playing this morning.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.850
-Huh? Seriously?

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.230
-I want to hear!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.450
They already started distributing it?

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.640
I know a site where they distribute it early.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:18.770
-How?!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.610
<i>Soon it will be a year since I started 
here at Kishimai High School.</i>

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.910
Now then, solve this problem... Shikishima.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:35.020
<i>If someone asked me whether I was 
happy right now, I'm sure—</i>

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:38.880
<i>No, before I give a direct answer,</i>

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.340
<i>let's think about what "happiness" is first.</i>

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.840
<i>For example, is it time spent 
with friends during breaks?</i>

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.470
<i>Is it being able to share different 
emotions with those friends?</i>

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.230
<i>Is it having a hobby one can get absorbed in?</i>

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.400
<b>Jungian Psychology</b>

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.400
<b>General Introduction to Psychology</b>

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.520
<i>Is it time spent enjoying beautiful music?</i>

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.320
<i>Is it having others acknowledge 
oneself and one's abilities?</i>

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.880
<i>Is "happiness" being able to recognize 
happiness is constituted of such things,</i>

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:14.000
<i>which frankly can be 
plentifully found at one's feet?</i>

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.740
<i>So if someone asked me whether I was 
happy with high school life,</i>

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.170
<b>Library</b>

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.170
<i>I would hold my chest out 
with pride and answer:</i>

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.600
I'm reading the same book he did again.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.140
Hey, let's go to a ramen shop!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.020
Ramen, again?

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.730
You really love it, Takatsu.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.390
When you're talking about high school 
guys, you think ramen, right?

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.370
It's part of our youth!

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.760
Really?

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.730
I don't think you'd call 
that enjoying our youth.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.840
I'm jealous.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.060
I'm not!

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.040
Hey, Ritsu, let's hurry up
 and hit the ramen shop!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:59.580
You know, sometimes bias causes myopia.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.890
There it is. Professor Shikishima's 
psychology lecture.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:05.150
"Myopia"? What's that?

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:08.880
The northern pike is a large, 
ugly freshwater fish,

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.650
but let's say we put it into an 
aquarium divided by a glass wall.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:16.240
Then, we unleash lots of 
small fish in the other side.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.310
The northern pike will rush 
forward to eat the small fish

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.770
and hit the glass wall.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.250
Afterward, even if you remove the glass wall,

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.660
the northern pike won't attack 
the small fish anymore.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.240
Because of its preconception.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:33.700
I don't understand.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.160
Uh, then...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.350
Imagine it's you inside the aquarium.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:41.520
It's cold.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.840
Now, let's say there's ramen on 
the other side of a glass wall.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.840
This is surreal.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.600
Takatsu-kun, you're dying to eat the ramen,

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.480
so you run into the glass wall and

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:51.140
make a bloody mess of yourself.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.480
Now afterward, even if the 
glass wall is removed,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:58.520
you'll think that glass wall is still there, 
so you'll hesitate to charge at it.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.980
I think I'd still charge at it.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.640
I mean, there's ramen there, right?

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.740
You might end up covered in blood again.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.310
So what?

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.950
I'd welcome getting covered in 
blood if it means eating ramen.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:15.080
Besides, there are no glass walls around us.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.370
Okay, you lose, professor!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.830
Ritsu, you overthink everything.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.360
Wait for me, ramen!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.380
Hey, wait up!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.050
-Come, let's go, Ritsu!

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.300
Thick, rich, with extra garlic!

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.260
<b>Meeting our customers 
leads to tomorrow's bowl.</b>

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:33.340
Here! This is the shop that comes 
highly recommend by gossip Narukonne!

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.560
Who's that?

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.680
The headphone girl in our class,
 Morita Naruko, right?

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.940
She's famous.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.060
See! She says the rich, pollack roe 
and pork belly butter ramen is superb!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:47.880
"It's a dream combination of fulsome 
pork belly and savory pollack roe."

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:53.540
"The two contrasting qualities 
form a yin and yang of creation."

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:57.030
"I tip my hat to their sense in combining 
these two incompatible flavors."

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.830
"It's truly chaos."

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:01.410
What is this?

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:02.540
Yes, it's here!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:03.670
It's hit me!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.850
That's a great review if I say so myself!

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:11.220
Thanks to me, this store is sure
 to have people lining up now!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.550
<b>Unusual Incidents Welcome!!</b>

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.630
<b>If you have interesting 
information, send it to me!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:12.930
<b>If you have interesting 
information, send it to me!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.010
<b>If you have interesting 
information, send it to me!

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:13.220
<b>Oh yeah, pawning it off on others now!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:13.260
<b>Oh yeah, pawning it off on others now!

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:13.510
<b>We're free

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:13.550
<b>We're free

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:13.680
<b>Oh, this morning I stepped on 
my grandfather's toothbrush.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:13.720
<b>Oh, this morning I stepped on 
my grandfather's toothbrush.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:13.800
<b>Oh, this morning I stepped on 
my grandfather's toothbrush.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.050
<b>Wow, harsh.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:14.180
<b>I'm so happy, I fell like I'm 
cloud nine from the big news!

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.710
Still hardly any reaction on this topic, huh?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.260
Hmm?

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.660
"My friend suddenly disappeared, 
but does anyone know anything?"

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.150
It's fishy! It's fishy!

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:27.860
It's fishy.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.360
This is damn good.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.240
Right?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.950
It's a harmony of savory pollack 
roe and fulsome pork belly!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.550
I'd definitely break that 
glass wall to get to the ramen!

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:46.040
Not bad.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.610
See? Right choice, wasn't it?

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.910
Way to go, Narukonne.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.190
The staff here are the ones making it.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:57.400
<i>Still, this smell seems familiar...</i>

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.860
Boss, seconds here, hard noodles!

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:01.500
Got it!

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.190
Same for me!

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.710
Got it! Two, hard!

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.570
Excessive consumption of carbohydrates is unhealthy.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.270
I have an extra stomach for ramen.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:12.780
It's good.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.040
Really? That's good.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.710
Mother, are you dieting again?

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:24.070
If I let my guard down for even a minute,
 I'll get fat in no time.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.080
You're lucky, Mifue.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.040
You don't gain weight from eating.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.180
Well, take your time and enjoy it, Mifue.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.740
What are you doing here?

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.890
Hey, is it fun here?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.500
Tell me, Mifue.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.320
Please.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.990
What?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.720
Aristotle? <i>On the Soul</i>?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:00.200
Have you started delving into philosophy, too?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.620
I thought I'd expand my perspective more.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.660
So, when do you think you can get it in?

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.200
Tomorrow.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:09.150
Books are good, but make sure you study, too.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.660
I know.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.960
Welcome home. Dinner's ready.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:22.080
Oh, I ate ramen on the way.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.320
What are you saying?

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:26.890
You high schoolers have separate 
stomachs for ramen, don't you?

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.290
This hurts...

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.180
I definitely ate too much.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:42.450
<i>My heartbeat resonates through the sky,</i>

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:47.450
<i>through endless, repeating days,</i>

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:55.020
<i>as I carry my hidden wounds.</i>

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:53.380
Something about that sensation...

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.090
What? Noise?

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.580
<i>Over and—</i>

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.350
<i>Please!</i>

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.220
<i>Stop μ!</i>

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.060
<i>Help me!</i>

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.440
What was that?

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.900
Mother, I'm home.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.030
Oh, welcome home, Mifue-chan.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.090
Dinner's almost ready.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.450
Let's eat together.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.060
It was cold out today, right?

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.950
So I'm making a stew.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.640
I wanted to eat some, too.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.330
I hope it turns out well.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.080
Right, Mifue-chan?

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.290
Mother?

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.010
<b>When you lose your composure, you 
cannot reach the truth or reality.</b>

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:50.800
What are you guys doing this weekend?

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:53.040
Oh, hey, let's go to that place, Sea Paraiso.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.790
"Sea Paraiso"? Never heard of it.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:54.860
Hey...

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.510
About μ's new song...

00:11:58.510 --> 00:11:59.930
It's a great song, right?

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:03.690
I can feel the sadness seeping into my heart.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.990
Yeah. So in that song, did you 
hear anything sounding like

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.330
spoken lines in the middle?

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.100
Like "help me" or something.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.470
Hey, answer me, guys.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.470
Hey, let's go for ramen again today.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.930
That shop from the other day was good.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.790
Come on, listen to this!

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:44.570
<i>My heartbeat resonates through the sky,</i>

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:51.980
What? What's gotten into you?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.010
Oh! It's the fighter, Satake Shogo!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.640
He's on another rampage!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.050
Hey, Morita-san!

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.100
Huh?! Toyama-kun? Hey!

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.950
Toyama-kun, what is it?

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.510
Are you aiming for the gain-loss effect?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.030
It's impossible.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.880
Hey? What do you think?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.410
Oh, hey! Wait!

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.610
A Johari Window always 
has the hidden window,

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:12.780
aspects of the self that you 
know but others don't.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.980
By revealing those aspects 
of yourself to others,

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:19.680
you can learn what others think of you.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:21.660
Then by spreading the open window,

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.830
you shine light on the other windows.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.090
According to Freud,

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:30.400
the conscious mind is only a 
fragment of a person's mind,

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.600
with the remaining majority being 
occupied by the subconscious.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.600
And some days, the subconscious 
will speak to the conscious mind.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:42.160
So don't you think we can interpret 
that as the voice of our hearts?

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.190
You're getting into complicated things again.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:48.990
Oh, uh, in other words, when the voice 
is completely different from my own,

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.670
or when I hear a voice I've never 
heard before talking to me,

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:58.400
or when everyone around me suddenly starts 
acting differently than I've known them to...

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.120
That's...

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.450
No, please forget about it.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.550
Thank you for the Aristotle.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.910
Books are good, but make sure you study, too.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:24.690
I don't understand.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.590
<i>Next up is the news.</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.070
<b>The Flower Festival Hosted Again This Year</b>

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.970
<i>The Flower Festival that 
draws huge crowds every year</i>

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.050
will be starting in Shikei Park.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.060
<i>μ will be performing on 
stage again this year,</i>

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:37.530
<i>and we can see the crowd is already 
getting excited before her performance.</i>

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.040
What on earth is going on?

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.460
<i>Incidentally, please view the 
special Flower Festival website</i>

